meta {
  name: Create Note
  type: http
  seq: 1
}

post {
  url: {{baseUrl}}/api/notes
  body: json
  auth: bearer
}

headers {
  Content-Type: application/json
}

auth:bearer {
  token: {{accessToken}}
}

body:json {
  {
    "entityType": "TRUCK",
    "entityId": {{truckId}},
    "categoryId": {{categoryId}},
    "content": "Tyre replaced at Nagpur, bill pending"
  }
}

script:post-response {
  bru.setEnvVar("noteId", res.body.data.id);
}

docs {
  Adds a top-level note on an entity (`NoteResource.createNote`, `common/controller/NoteResource.java`,
  service `NoteService.createNote`). Notes are generic: `entityType` + `entityId` say what the note is
  on. Only `TRUCK` is supported today.

  Roles: every torg role except DRIVER (VAHN_ADMIN, TORG_ADMIN, MANAGER, TRUCK_MANAGER,
  FUND_MANAGER, ACCOUNTANT, OPERATOR, AGENT). The caller must be able to see the truck.
  The note belongs to the caller's torg, and only that torg's users see it. VAHN_ADMIN has no torg, so
  it must add `?torgId=<id>`.

  Set `truckId` (and `accessToken`) in the selected environment first. The created note's id is saved
  to `noteId` for the other requests in this folder.

  Every response is HTTP 200 with the real code in the body's `statusCode` (the API wrapper does this
  for errors too, so check the body). Success returns the note in `data`: `id`, `torgId`, `entityType`, `entityId`, `parentNoteId`, `rootNoteId`, `depth`, `content`,
  `category {id, name}`, `author {id, name, role, image, imageUrl}`, `createdAt`, `editedAt`, `edited`,
  `editableUntil`, `deleted`, `canEdit`, `canDelete`, `replyCount`, `attachments [{id, key, fileName, contentType, size, url}]`. `url` is a short-lived
  signed link; fetch the note again once it has expired.

  `categoryId` is required on a top-level truck note: one of "List Note Categories" (run it first; it
  saves the first category to `categoryId`). Replies don't need one.

  `author.image` is the profile image storage key (`User.image`) and `imageUrl` a short-lived link to it,
  only for `profile_pic/...` keys (null otherwise).
  `editableUntil` is when the author loses edit/delete (trucks: 15 minutes after creation); null for
  entity types without a time limit.

  Optional `attachments: [{key, fileName, contentType, size}]`: files already uploaded with "Upload
  Attachment" (folder `notes/<torgId>`). Trucks allow at most 10. See "Create Note With Attachment".

  Truck notes can be edited and deleted only by the author, and only within 15 minutes of being added;
  `canEdit`/`canDelete` already reflect that at the time of the response.

  400 if `entityType`/`entityId` is missing, the truck isn't visible to the caller, or VAHN_ADMIN sent no
  `torgId`, or `categoryId` is missing ("categoryId is required for a TRUCK note") or not a live truck
  category ("Unknown category for TRUCK: <id>"). 404 "Vehicle not found" for an unknown truck. 400 "content is required" or "content must be at
  most 2000 characters" for blank or over-long `content`. 400 for more than 10 attachments, a key outside
  `notes/<torgId>/`, a file missing from storage, or the same file twice. Success is body `statusCode`
  200, not 201.
}
